ri material culture among local populations by saying that the Wari were an empire whose pottery was so powerful that withholding it from local people made them compliant on the hopes that they might some day be invited to come to a Wari site to see it.  Of course, from that interpretation, there are a lot of cultures that are absent from the Andes, and an empirical field of archaeology can’t really make any real contribution without working with patterns that are actually present." (R. Alan Covey, pers. comm. to R. Ainsworth, June 2023)'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1936, 'temperature': 0.2})
